The daemon reads each registered repo's (repos.toml) kinds every minute from its main (`origin/main` after a fetch when the repo has an `origin`, else `main`) and starts, restarts or stops pools to match. A registered repo whose path does not exist on this box (a row for another box) is skipped, with no kinds here, and logged once per daemon start: `routines: repo has no checkout on this box; skipped repo=<name> path=<path>`. A kind whose `os` on main is set and isn't the box's own OS is left out: that daemon starts no feed for it, writes no consumer settings and starts no instances, so it never fetches the kind's jobs and only a box of that OS runs them. Routines are off when `[runner] checkouts` is empty.
